reased G-quadruplex formation at specific...", "display_url": "nature.com/articles/s4155…", "end": 163, "expanded_url": "https://www.nature.com/articles/s41556-026-02126-0", "images": [{"height": 1628, "url": "https://pbs.twimg.com/news_img/2118448921223819264/G1pawCXp?format=jpg&name=orig", "width": 2166}, {"height": 150, "url": "https://pbs.twimg.com/news_img/2118448921223819264/G1pawCXp?format=jpg&name=150x150", "width": 150}], "start": 140, "status": 200, "title": "Positional replication fork instability drives PARP inhibitor cytotoxicity", "unwound_url": "https://www.nature.com/articles/s41556-026-02126-0?error=cookies_not_supported&code=878b142c-2608-48fd-b713-eaa1182d8fb0", "url": "https://t.co/kG9wSiDgm5"}]}, "id": "2118448912323535271", "public_metrics": {"bookmark_count": 0, "impression_count": 73, "like_count": 1, "quote_count": 0, "reply_count": 0, "retweet_count": 0}, "text": "CRISPRスクリーニングと単一分子解析から、コヒーシンアセチル化酵素ESCO2の欠損が特定領域でG-quadruplex形成と複製フォーク不安定性を高め、PARP活性化を介してPARP阻害薬への高感受性をもたらすことを示した論文がNat Cell Biol誌に発表されました。\nhttps://t.co/kG9wSiDgm5", "url": "https://x.com/iPatho1/status/2118448912323535271"}, {"author_id": "1428911804781056004", "created_at": "2026-11-05T21:06:51.000Z", "edit_history_tweet_ids": ["2118449992201625998"], "entities": {"urls": [{"display_url": "pic.x.com/DxGwXDLn7v", "end": 300, "expanded_url": "https://x.com/ValerieAnne1970/status/2118449992201625998/photo/1", "media_key": "3_2118449986471858176", "start": 277, "url": "https://t.co/DxGwXDLn7v"}]}, "id": "2118449992201625998", "public_metrics": {"bookmark_count": 22, "impression_count": 2568, "like_count": 53, "quote_count": 0, "reply_count": 5, "retweet_count": 43}, "text": "You think you're just eating \"cheese\"?  \n\nThink again.  \n\n~90% of American cheese uses a lab-engineered FAKE RENNET called FPC (fermentation-produced chymosin) — originally developed and PATENTED BY PFIZER in 1990.  \n\nToday’s version is made by splicing the calf chymosin gene https://t.co/DxGwXDLn7v", "